tvmount is a small command-line calculator for hanging a TV on a wall.
From the screen diagonal and the seating position it works out the
mount height, the vertical viewing angle, the screen size range for
the seat (SMPTE 30 to THX 40 degrees), the downward tilt needed above
a fireplace or mantel, and the anchor, drill bit and wiring method for
a wall type (wood or steel studs, masonry, stucco, plaster). It also
checks a TV's VESA pattern against the screen size and a mount's range
and weight limit.

Examples:
  tvmount height --diagonal 65 --distance 132 --fireplace --mantel 52
  tvmount wall brick
  tvmount vesa 400x300 --diagonal 65 --mount-max 600x400

Every command accepts --json; lengths can be given in cm with
--units cm. See tvmount(1).

The python module (import tvmount) is installed as well.
